          "number": 10,
          "question": "When graphing a half-plane, when do you draw a dashed boundary line and when do you draw a solid boundary line?",
          "answer": "Use a dashed line for strict inequalities ($<$ or $>$) where points on the line are excluded, and a solid line for $\\le$ or $\\ge$ where points on the line are included."
